csv:     pit-screen-recovery.csv
source:  source.pdf p.10 (report page -6-); DTIC AD0702233
anchor:  Fragments caught by following screens:
anchor:  Pit Fragmentation Tests of 75 mm T3 Shell from 75 mm

# Tolch (1938), BRL Report 126 -- sand-pit fragmentation test, fragments
# recovered on each retaining screen, AVERAGED OVER THE FOUR ROUNDS ("Ave. of
# 4 rds."). The per-round table is on the facing page (report page -5-).
#
# SHELL IDENTITY: this is the same shell as the panel tests. The report is
# titled "FRAGMENTATION EFFECTS OF THE 75MM H.E. SHELL T3 (M48)" -- T3 is the
# developmental designation of the M48, not a different projectile. The
# 105 mm M1 results are explicitly "reserved for a separate report".
#
# CLOSURE INVARIANTS -- the source prints a total row beneath the five screen
# rows, and prints two percentage columns whose bases it states in the column
# headings. All four checks are non-vacuous: the totals are separately typeset
# from the rows they sum, and each percentage is a ratio of two other printed
# columns.
#
#   1. the five screen counts sum to the printed total, 779;
#   2. `pct_no` is each row's share of that total  ("% of total no. of
#      fragments");
#   3. `pct_empty` is each row's weight over the empty shell & fuze weight
#      ("% of empty shell & fuze"). That divisor is 13.29 lb -- the mean of
#      the four per-round values 13.29 / 13.29 / 13.26 / 13.33 tabulated on
#      report page -5- (anchor "Wt. empty shell"), NOT a fitted constant;
#   4. the printed column totals (779 / 100.0 / 12.708 / 95.6) each reproduce
#      as the sum of their column.
#
# All hold to the printed 1-3 d.p. on all five rows.
#
# WHY 779 AND NOT 803: committed model artifacts under
# experiment/fragmentation-field/ quote the recovered count as 803. The
# `pct_no` column discriminates: at N=779 every row reproduces its printed
# percentage, at N=803 screens 2 and "thru 4" miss theirs by 1.03 and 0.45 pp
# -- far outside the 0.05 pp rounding band the other rows sit in. 779 is also
# what the report's own body text states (report page -74-, anchor "In the pit
# fragmentation tests, an average of"). See
# experiment/fragmentation-field/challenges/source-data-audit/checks/
# tolch-count-basis-closure.py.
#
# Not transcribed: the per-round table on report page -5-, whose screen-4 and
# recovered-count glyphs are damaged in this scan. The averaged table here is
# legible and carries its own closure, so the per-round table is not needed by
# any current consumer.
row:    pct_no - 100 * n_frag / 779 == 0 within 0.06
row:    pct_empty - 100 * wt_lb / 13.29 == 0 within 0.06
total:  n_frag == 779 within 0.5
total:  pct_no == 100.0 within 0.15
total:  wt_lb == 12.708 within 0.005
total:  pct_empty == 95.6 within 0.15
